  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/883977f7-5f8e-45aa-86e9-cce9dc15ea3b-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 183px;\" /></p><p>As the block moves with constant velocity, so force on the block should be balanced. The forces acting on the block are its weight, normal contact force and&nbsp;friction. The contact force is vector sum of normal contact and friction. As the forces are balanced, the contact force should be equal and opposite to its weight.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>Contact force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
